From 433439b2c99385d4bfa8f1ef64581941bedaf80d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:18:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ntr/hal: dry frames make no vertices and light a NORMAL only
 when it is seen

A dry frame (gx_frame_dry) skipped the vertices of replayed lists only;
every other list still recorded its vertices and lit every NORMAL. Now
vertex() makes nothing on a dry frame, a NORMAL there is lit only before a
command that reads or changes what it leaves (nrm_before), a dry frame keeps
no list, and engine A's fade is not run. The game's reads stay exact (Azahar,
levels 1, 6, 8 with GAME3DS_DRY=2: every [ltrace] line the same).
normal_light: one divide, not three. The memos' sums (lm_sum, memo_sum) in
three lanes: two FNV over the even and odd words, a rotate-add.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 port/hal/message_compositor.cpp |  25 ++-
 port/ntr/gx.cpp                 | 264 +++++++++++++++++++-------------
 2 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 111 deletions(-)

